        role: "Resident",
        exam: [.direct("What did you see from your window?", "\"{D} with a knife in the apartment lot. I saw {V} get stabbed, and then {DL} left.\""), .direct("How many times was {V} stabbed?", "\"Three times, according to the medical report. I saw it happen from a distance.\""), .direct("How was {D} found?", "\"By tracking a cab. A cab receipt shows a ride from the scene.\""), .direct("How is the apartment lot laid out?", "\"A paved lot behind the building with two rows of parked cars and a single light by the dumpsters. Many residents' windows face it.\""), .direct("What did you see that night?", "\"Two people were arguing near a car. One pulled something out and swung it at the other, and the person went down.\""), .direct("What did you do?", "\"I stood frozen at my window, then called when the attacker left. Several of us were watching.\""), .cross("Did {V} attack the defendant first?", "\"I saw movement before the stabbing, but I could not tell who started it. It was dark.\""), .cross("Why did no one call right away?", "\"We were frozen. Many of us watched, and no one called until the attacker left.\""), .cross("Did the defendant have any visible injury?", "\"I did not see one. I was too far away.\""), .cross("You did not see who threw the first punch, did you?", "\"No. They were facing away from my window and I saw only the arms.\""), .cross("The lot is dim, isn't it?", "\"Yes. There is one light, and the area around the cars is shadowed.\"")],
        defenseRole: "ER nurse",
