        exam: [.direct("What did you review in {D}'s claim files?", "\"Eleven spinal procedures billed for $210,000. I reviewed the files for medical necessity.\""), .direct("What did second opinions say?", "\"No surgical need. Specialists found that the patients did not need those operations.\""), .direct("What did you notice about the scans?", "\"Scans in the files belonged to other patients. They were mismatched to the people being billed.\""), .direct("What is your role?", "\"I am a medical reviewer for the insurer, reviewing claims for surgical need. I am a licensed orthopedic surgeon myself.\""), .direct("What stood out about the defendant's claims?", "\"Eleven spinal fusions in about a year, all billed at high rates. The symptoms in the charts did not match the severity of the procedures.\""), .direct("What did the scans show?", "\"In several files, the scans carried a different patient's name and date. A comparison with imaging from the hospital showed no structural problem for the actual patients.\""), .cross("Surgeons often disagree on whether to operate, don't they?", "\"Yes. Judgment calls differ. But these were not close calls, and the scans were wrong.\""), .cross("Did a colleague approve any of the cases?", "\"Yes, a colleague approved two. That much is true.\""), .cross("Could the scans have been misfiled?", "\"It is possible. Misfiling happens. But the pattern was concerning.\""), .cross("A fusion can sometimes help for chronic pain, can't it?", "\"It can, but only after failed conservative care. Most of these patients never had physical therapy first.\""), .cross("The two approved by a colleague had matching scans, didn't they?", "\"Yes. I accepted those, which is why I flagged only nine.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Colleague surgeon",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Did you approve any of {D}'s cases?", "\"Two. I reviewed them and found the surgeries reasonable at the time.\""), .direct("Why did you approve those two?", "\"The patients had real symptoms, and the surgeries were within accepted practice. I stand by those two.\""), .direct("Did you review the others?", "\"No. I did not see the others. I only know about the two I approved.\""), .direct("What is your specialty?", "\"Orthopedic spine surgery. I work at the same hospital as {D} and consult on difficult cases.\""), .direct("What cases did you review for the defendant?", "\"Two patients with clear nerve compression and failed therapy. I agreed that surgery was reasonable.\""), .direct("What did you see in the imaging?", "\"Disc herniation and narrowing that matched the symptoms. The scans were the right patients' scans.\""), .cross("Did you review the scans for those two?", "\"Yes. They matched the patients. I do not know about the others.\""), .cross("Are you friends with the defendant?", "\"We work together. I respect {DF}, but I only speak to the cases I saw.\""), .cross("Would you approve eleven spinal surgeries in a short span?", "\"That would be a lot. I would want to look at each more carefully.\""), .cross("You did not review nine of the eleven cases, did you?", "\"No, only the two I was asked about.\""), .cross("Eleven in a year would give you pause, wouldn't it?", "\"It would make me look at each case closely.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} billed for unneeded surgery.", "Judgment calls."),
        allocution: "\"I believed in the work.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} had a surgery quota in a contract.", "A colleague approved two of the cases."),
        defendant: [.direct("Were those surgeries necessary?", "\"I thought so. I believed the patients would benefit from the procedures, and I made my best judgment.\""), .direct("Why were the scans for other patients?", "\"Filing errors. The staff filed scans in the wrong charts, and I did not catch it.\""), .direct("Did you have a surgery quota?", "\"Yes, in a contract. I was expected to perform a certain number, but I did not operate to meet it.\""), .direct("What is your approach to spine surgery?", "\"I operate when conservative treatment has failed and the patient has persistent pain or nerve symptoms. I try to be conservative.\""), .direct("How do you review scans?", "\"My staff attaches them to the chart, and I view them on a monitor before the procedure. I look at the image, not the label.\""), .direct("What about the quota?", "\"My contract had a minimum number of procedures per year. It never changed my decision on a patient.\""), .cross("Eleven procedures, $210,000, and second opinions say none was needed. How is that judgment?", "\"Doctors differ. I made calls I believed in.\""), .cross("A quota in your contract might make you want more surgeries, mightn't it?", "\"It could. I was aware of it. I tried not to let it affect me.\""), .cross("Scans from other patients were in the files. How do you explain that?", "\"Staff errors. I did not review every scan. That is on me.\""), .cross("Eleven spinal procedures in a year is a lot, isn't it?", "\"It is a busy year, and I had a long wait list.\""), .cross("A quota in your contract could push anyone toward surgery, couldn't it?", "\"I understand that concern. I believe I kept it out of my judgment.\"")],
        openings: ("{D}, a surgeon, billed $210,000 for eleven spinal procedures that second opinions say were unnecessary, with scans in the files belonging to other patients. {D}'s contract carried a quota.", "Jurors will hear that surgeons honestly differ on when to operate, that a colleague approved two of these cases, and that the scans were filing errors."),
        closings: ("Eleven surgeries, $210,000 billed, scans from other patients, and a quota in the contract. Patients were operated on without need, and {D} profited from every one.", "Medicine involves judgment, and a colleague approved two of these cases. The State must prove {D} knew the surgeries were unnecessary, and a disagreement is not that."),
