        exam: [.direct("What did {D} do at your events?", "\"{D} attended eleven events where {V}, a local chef, appeared. {DL} also posted {V}'s location online each time.\""), .direct("What do the event cameras show?", "\"{DL} at each event. The videos are clear, and the timing lines up with the posts.\""), .direct("What warning had been given?", "\"{V} had sent a written request to stop. A warning letter is in our file.\""), .direct("What kind of events does {V} appear at?", "\"Pop-up dinners, farmers market demos, and charity tastings around the region. I book most of them and manage the guest lists.\""), .direct("How did you first notice the defendant?", "\"At the third event, I recognized {D.him} from the first two. {D.He} stood near the demo table and took pictures of {V} and the stage.\""), .direct("What did {V} do about it?", "\"{V} sent a written request asking {DL} to stop following and posting locations. {DL} came to the next event anyway.\""), .cross("Did the defendant buy tickets openly?", "\"Yes. {D.He} bought tickets and entered like any guest. {D.He} did not sneak in.\""), .cross("{D} says {D.he} is a fan, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"That is what {D.he} says. Many fans come to see {V}, and that is not unusual.\""), .cross("Did the defendant threaten anyone?", "\"No. There were no threats. It was the following and the posting that worried us.\""), .cross("{D} never spoke to {V} at any event, did {D.he}?", "\"Not that I saw. {DL} kept a distance and stood at the back.\""), .cross("The posts did not include {V}'s home address, did they?", "\"No. They gave the event locations, which are public.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Ticket seller",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Did {D} buy tickets to the events?", "\"Always. {D} bought a ticket every time and paid full price at the window, like any other guest.\""), .direct("Was the defendant polite at the events you saw?", "\"Yes. {D.He} was polite and quiet. {D.He} did not cause any trouble at the door or inside that I saw.\""), .direct("Did you ever tell {D} that {V} wanted {D} to stay away?", "\"No. It was not my job to tell anyone that. I only sold tickets at the window.\""), .direct("What is your role at events?", "\"I sell tickets at the entrance and check names. I have worked many of {V}'s events.\""), .direct("What do you remember about the defendant?", "\"A polite regular who always arrived early, paid, and moved on. I never saw anything rude.\""), .direct("Did you see the defendant do anything unusual?", "\"Only that {D.he} came to a lot of events. Fans do that for popular chefs.\""), .cross("Did you know about the written letter asking {D} to stop?", "\"No. I did not know about the letter until afterward, when I heard about it from others.\""), .cross("How often did you see the defendant at the ticket window?", "\"At many events. I remember the face, because {D.he} was a regular and always came early.\""), .cross("Did the defendant seem to you to be following {V} from place to place?", "\"I do not know. I saw {DF} in line like any other fan, and nothing beyond that.\""), .cross("You did not know about the warning, did you?", "\"No. The organizer did not tell the ticket staff.\""), .cross("You cannot say what the defendant did after leaving the ticket line, can you?", "\"No. I stayed at the entrance.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} stalked a chef.", "A fan."),
        allocution: "\"I went too far.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} drove two hours each time.", "{DL} bought tickets openly."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you stalk {V}?", "\"No. I am a fan. I like {V}'s cooking and I attended events to see {V.him}.\""), .direct("Why did you post {V}'s location?", "\"I wanted other fans to know where {V} would be. I did not think it would scare anyone.\""), .direct("How far did you travel?", "\"Two hours each way. I bought tickets every time and went openly.\""), .direct("How did you become a fan?", "\"I tried {V}'s food at a festival and loved it. I started following the schedule on social media and went to events whenever I could.\""), .direct("What did you post?", "\"Photos of the dishes and the location and time of the next event, for other fans. I did not intend to tell anyone where {V} lived.\""), .direct("What did you think when you got the letter?", "\"I felt embarrassed and thought it was a misunderstanding. I did not stop right away because I did not believe I was bothering anyone.\""), .cross("{V} asked you to stop in writing, didn't {V.he}?", "\"Yes. I got the letter. I should have stopped. I did not take it seriously.\""), .cross("Eleven events and eleven posts. Isn't that following?", "\"I understand how it looks. I was a fan and did not mean harm.\""), .cross("You drove two hours each time to see one person?", "\"Yes. I admired {V}. I did not think I was bothering anyone.\""), .cross("You kept going after the letter, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I went to two more events after it arrived, and I regret that.\""), .cross("Eleven events in two hours' driving distance is a lot of time, isn't it?", "\"Yes. It was a big part of my free time, and I did not see how it looked to {V}.\"")],
        openings: ("{D} followed {V}, a local chef, to eleven events and posted {V}'s location online each time, after receiving a written request to stop. {D} drove two hours to each event.", "The defense witnesses will explain that {D} is a fan who bought tickets openly, threatened no one, and did not understand that the posts frightened {V}."),
        closings: ("Eleven events, eleven location posts, a written request to stop, and a camera showing {D} at every event. That is not fandom.", "A fan who bought tickets openly and posted about events. The State must prove {D} meant to harass {V}, and admiration is not harassment."),
        timeline: [(-60, "The first event."), (-7, "The warning."), (0, "The eleventh."), (30, "Charges.")],
        identified: "Event cameras.",
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        impact: "I stopped announcing my schedule.",
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"],
        genders: ["D": .male, "V": .female])

    static let syrupReserveHeist = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.syrupReserveHeist",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Trucker Hauled Off a Tanker of Maple Syrup Stored for Farmers", "Syrup Turns Up Relabeled in Three States"],
        law: "felonyLarceny",
        threshold: 6,
        spec: "Took and carried away property of {V} worth over $1,000, on or about {DATE}.",
        ages: 25...65,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{D}, a trucker, hauled a tanker holding $190,000 of stored maple syrup from {V}'s warehouse on {DATE} and sold it through a broker. {DL} says the warehouse manager hired {D.him} to move it. The tanker left the gate at 3 a.m., three days after a phone call to {D}. The broker sold the syrup a week later, and the warehouse audit found it missing after three weeks.",
        state: [E(.document, 3, "Gate Log", "Tanker left at 3 a.m."), E(.digital, 3, "Broker Texts", "{D} offers 'barrels' at half price."), E(.forensic, 2, "Sample Match", "Syrup in three states matches the warehouse lot.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Work Order", "{DL} shows a phone order to move the tanker.")],
        role: "Warehouse manager",
        exam: [.direct("What happened at your warehouse?", "\"A tanker holding $190,000 of maple syrup left the gate at 3 a.m., three days after a phone call to {D}.\""), .direct("What did your sample match show?", "\"Syrup sold in three states matched our warehouse lot. The broker sold it a week later.\""), .direct("How is the syrup stored?", "\"In a stainless tanker parked in a locked yard at the back of the warehouse. Each load has a lot number and a seal.\""), .direct("What does the gate log show?", "\"A tanker pulling out at 3:02 a.m., with {D.his} truck number and no outbound order. The gate guard is not on at that hour, and the log is automatic.\""), .direct("How did you trace the syrup?", "\"A broker contacted a buyer in three states, and samples sent to us matched the lot. The texts show {DL} offering barrels at half price.\""), .direct("How much syrup was missing when you checked the tanker bay?", "\"The tanker held roughly $190,000 of stored syrup and it was empty. The bay was cold and clean, and no one had logged a transfer or a delivery.\""), .cross("{D} says you hired {D.him} to move it, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"Yes. {DL} says that. I did phone {DL} the night before the tanker left.\""), .cross("Was the load on the books?", "\"No. The load was not on the books. That is a problem for both of us.\""), .cross("How long before you noticed the loss?", "\"About three weeks. The warehouse audit found it missing.\""), .cross("You did phone the defendant the night before, didn't you?", "\"I phoned {D.him} about another matter. I did not authorize a pickup.\""), .cross("The syrup was sold a week later, wasn't it?", "\"Yes, by the broker. {D.He} delivered and then was paid in cash.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Dispatcher",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Was the load on the books?", "\"No. I did not see it on our dispatch schedule. It was not logged as a job.\""), .direct("Did {D} ask about work that week?", "\"Once. {D} called to ask if there was any hauling available, and I said I would check.\""), .direct("Did you assign the defendant that load?", "\"No. I did not. I had no record of it.\""), .direct("What is your role?", "\"I am the dispatcher at the trucking company. I assign jobs, track loads, and keep records.\""), .direct("Did you assign the defendant to the syrup load?", "\"No. It never came through dispatch, and I had no paperwork on it.\""), .direct("How could the defendant have gotten the job?", "\"Perhaps by a direct call from the warehouse. It happens but is not the way it should be done.\""), .cross("Did the warehouse manager call the defendant?", "\"I do not know. I only know what the schedule said.\""), .cross("Could a job be arranged without the dispatcher?", "\"It can happen informally. It is not supposed to.\""), .cross("Do you know why the tanker left at 3 a.m.?", "\"No. That is an odd hour. I would not have scheduled it.\""), .cross("You do not know who called {D}, do you?", "\"No. I only know it was not me.\""), .cross("A 3 a.m. pickup would be unusual, wouldn't it?", "\"Yes, that hour is unusual, and I would have asked questions.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} drove off with the syrup.", "A verbal order."),
        allocution: "\"I should have asked for paper.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} sold it at half price to a broker.", "The manager did phone {DL} the night before."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you steal the syrup?", "\"No. I was hired to move it. The warehouse manager called me and arranged the haul.\""), .direct("Why did you leave at 3 a.m.?", "\"The roads are cheaper at that hour, with less traffic and no tolls. It is how I run loads.\""), .direct("Did you sell the syrup?", "\"No. I did not sell it. I delivered it, and I did not know what happened after.\""), .direct("What is your work?", "\"I haul bulk liquids in a tanker for hire. Dispatchers call me with jobs, and sometimes owners do too.\""), .direct("What did the manager say on the phone?", "\"That there was a load of syrup to move that needed to go fast, and that the paperwork would follow. I took it at face value.\""), .direct("Why was it half price?", "\"The broker found a buyer who wanted a quick sale, and I passed along the offer. I assumed the manager had arranged it.\""), .cross("Your texts offer 'barrels' at half price to a broker, don't they?", "\"It was a rush job, and I passed along a deal. I did not own the syrup.\""), .cross("Syrup from the warehouse was sold in three states. Who sold it?", "\"A broker did.\""), .cross("The load was not on the books. Didn't that tell you something?", "\"I trusted the manager's call. I should have checked.\""), .cross("You took no paperwork with you, did you?", "\"I never got any. I knew that was odd, but I was in a hurry.\""), .cross("You were paid by the broker, weren't you?", "\"Yes, in cash. I did not question it.\"")],
        openings: ("A tanker holding $190,000 of stored maple syrup left a warehouse gate at 3 a.m., three days after the manager phoned {D}, a trucker. The syrup was sold through a broker at half price.", "Listen for the defense evidence, which will show that the manager phoned {D} and asked {D} to move the load, and that {D} believed the job was legitimate."),
        closings: ("A 3 a.m. departure, an off-the-books load, texts offering syrup at half price, and a sample match in three states. The syrup was stolen.", "A phone call from the manager, a hauling job, and a rush. The State must prove {D} knew the load was not authorized."),
        timeline: [(-3, "A phone call to {DL}."), (0, "3 a.m.: tanker leaves."), (7, "Broker sells."), (21, "Audit finds it missing.")],
        identified: "Gate log.",
        mood: .indifferent,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"])

    static let reptileHoardCruelty = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.reptileHoardCruelty",
        category: .publicOrder,
        headlines: ["Breeder Kept Dozens of Exotic Reptiles in Unheated Sheds", "Animal Control Finds Dead and Starving Animals"],
        law: "animalCruelty",
        threshold: 7,
        spec: "Intentionally and without justification failed to provide necessary sustenance and shelter to animals, on or about {DATE}.",
        ages: 22...65,
        victim: false,
        summary: "{D} kept about 90 exotic reptiles in sheds with no heat on {DATE}. Officers found 31 dead. {DL} says the heater failed that week.",
        state: [E(.forensic, 3, "Veterinary Report", "Cold stress and starvation."), E(.video, 3, "Shed Photos", "Empty water dishes."), E(.document, 2, "Feed Receipts", "No purchases for five weeks.")],
        defense: [E(.document, 1, "Heater Invoice", "{DL} ordered a replacement heater.")],
        role: "Animal control officer",
        exam: [.direct("What did you find in {D}'s sheds when you arrived?", "\"About 90 exotic reptiles in sheds with no heat at all. Thirty-one of them were already dead when we got there.\""), .direct("What did the veterinary report conclude about the animals?", "\"Cold stress and starvation. The animals had gone without proper heat and food for a long stretch of time.\""), .direct("What did the feed receipts show about purchases?", "\"No purchases for five weeks. That means no feed was bought during that period, and the dishes were empty.\""), .direct("What did you see on arrival?", "\"Several sheds behind a house with doors shut, and the temperature inside around forty degrees. Racks of glass tanks were stacked floor to ceiling.\""), .direct("What condition were the animals in?", "\"Thin, lethargic, and many with sunken eyes. We found 31 dead on the shelves and in the cages, and the rest needed treatment.\""), .direct("What about food and water?", "\"Water dishes were dry and crusted, and the feeder insects were gone. The last feed store receipt was five weeks old.\""), .cross("{D} says the heater failed that week, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"Yes. A heater order is dated before the cold arrived, and I will say that does appear in the records.\""), .cross("Did {D} answer when you called or came to the property?", "\"Eventually, yes. {D} was cooperative once we arrived and helped us move animals to safety.\""), .cross("How many animals survived the neglect?", "\"Fifty-nine survived. Many of them needed treatment, and some are still recovering with our veterinarian.\""), .cross("The owner did let you in, didn't the defendant?", "\"Yes, {D.he} opened the sheds and answered questions. I did not have to force entry.\""), .cross("A broken heater can happen to anyone, can't it?", "\"Yes. But the heater order was before the cold, and nothing explains the empty dishes.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Hobbyist",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Did {D} answer your messages that week?", "\"Not that week. I sent several messages and heard nothing back from {D} until a few days later.\""), .direct("Did the defendant ever mention a heater problem to you?", "\"Yes. {D.He} said a heater had been ordered and was on its way, and that the shed was getting cold.\""), .direct("How did the defendant usually care for the animals?", "\"Carefully. I have seen the sheds before, and the animals were in much better shape in those earlier visits.\""), .direct("How do you know the defendant?", "\"We belong to the same reptile hobby group and trade animals. I have been to {D.his} sheds twice.\""), .direct("How did the defendant keep the sheds?", "\"Clean, with heat mats and thermostats. The animals looked healthy when I visited last year.\""), .direct("What did {D} tell you about the heater?", "\"That it had failed and that a replacement was on order. {D.He} sounded stressed.\""), .cross("Did you personally see the animals in the last few weeks?", "\"No. I did not visit that month, so I cannot say what the sheds looked like then.\""), .cross("Did you know how many animals the defendant kept in total?", "\"About ninety. Many of us in the hobby knew that number, and some thought it was too many.\""), .cross("Did the defendant keep buying new animals during that time?", "\"I heard that {D.he} bought some new ones. I do not know how many or when exactly.\""), .cross("You have not been there in the last month, have you?", "\"No. I could not say how the animals were that month.\""), .cross("Ninety animals is a lot for one person, isn't it?", "\"It is, even for an experienced keeper.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} let animals starve and freeze.", "A heater failure."),
        allocution: "\"I took on too many.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} kept buying new animals while old ones went unfed.", "The heater order is dated before the cold."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you feed the reptiles each day?", "\"Daily. I fed them every single day until a stretch where everything fell apart and I fell behind.\""), .direct("How many animals did you have at that time?", "\"About ninety. It was too many for one person to handle, and I know that now, looking back.\""), .direct("Why were the sheds without heat that week?", "\"The heater failed that week. I had ordered a new one, but it had not arrived when the cold came.\""), .direct("How did your collection grow?", "\"I started with a few snakes and kept adding species until I had about ninety. I loved them and could not say no to a rescue.\""), .direct("What happened with the heater?", "\"The main unit in the biggest shed broke during a cold snap. I ordered a replacement and waited for it to arrive.\""), .direct("What did you do for the animals in the meantime?", "\"I put space heaters in some sheds and moved a few animals indoors. It was not enough for the rest.\""), .cross("You bought new animals while older ones went unfed, didn't you?", "\"A few new ones. I know how that looks. I was overextended and I made poor choices about priorities.\""), .cross("No feed purchases for five weeks. How did you feed them?", "\"I had some supplies left over. It was not enough, and I should have bought more or asked for help.\""), .cross("Thirty-one animals are dead. Do you accept responsibility for that?", "\"Yes, I do. I am heartbroken about it, and I should have asked someone for help sooner.\""), .cross("You kept buying new animals while old ones went hungry, didn't you?", "\"I bought a few new animals in that stretch, and that was a failure of priorities.\""), .cross("Thirty-one animals died on your watch, didn't they?", "\"Yes. I will carry that with me.\"")],
        openings: ("Officers found about 90 exotic reptiles in unheated sheds with empty water dishes, and 31 were dead. A veterinarian found cold stress and starvation, and feed receipts show no purchases for five weeks.", "The defense case is that the heater failed that week, that a replacement was ordered before the cold, and that {D} cared for the animals daily."),
        closings: ("Ninety reptiles, no heat, empty water dishes, five weeks without feed, and thirty-one dead. Animals depend entirely on their keeper, and {D} failed them.", "A heater that failed and a replacement already on order before the cold. The State must prove {D} knowingly let the animals suffer, and bad luck with equipment is not that."),
        timeline: [(-35, "Last feed receipt."), (-5, "Heater breaks."), (0, "Officers arrive."), (10, "Charges.")],
        identified: "Seized animals.",
        mood: .sympathetic,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"])

    static let brotherNameForTwentyYears = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.brotherNameForTwentyYears",
        category: .whiteCollar,
        headlines: ["Man Lived Two Decades Under His Late Brother's Name", "Benefits and Loans Taken in the Dead Man's Name"],
        law: "identityTheft",
        threshold: 7,
        spec: "Knowingly obtained and used the identifying information of a deceased relative, to avoid legal processes and obtain benefits, on or about {DATE}.",
        ages: 40...70,
        victim: false,
        summary: "{D} used the name and number of a dead relative, to hold jobs, claim $140,000 in benefits and take a mortgage. {DL} says the family asked {D.him} to carry on the name. The relative died about twenty-five years earlier, and {D} took the name about twenty years ago. The benefit claims and the mortgage were paid and signed in that name until a bank flagged the file.",
        state: [E(.document, 3, "Death Record", "The relative died years earlier."), E(.digital, 3, "Benefit Claims", "Paid in the dead relative's name."), E(.document, 2, "Mortgage File", "Signed with the dead relative's number.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Family Letter", "A letter from relatives.")],
        role: "Fraud investigator",
        exam: [.direct("What did you find about {DL}'s identity?", "\"{D} used the name and number of a dead relative to hold jobs, claim $140,000 in benefits, and take a mortgage.\""), .direct("When did the relative die?", "\"About twenty-five years earlier. {D.He} took the name about twenty years ago, and used it until a bank flagged the file.\""), .direct("What do the files show?", "\"Benefit claims paid in the dead relative's name, and a mortgage signed with that number.\""), .direct("How was this case discovered?", "\"A bank flagged a mortgage application because the Social Security number belonged to a person listed as deceased. Our unit opened an investigation.\""), .direct("What did your review show?", "\"{D.He} had held jobs, filed taxes, and collected $140,000 in benefits under the name and number of a relative who died about twenty-five years earlier.\""), .direct("What did {D} say?", "\"{D.He} said the family had asked {D.him} to carry on the name. {D.He} gave me a letter signed by several relatives.\""), .cross("{DL} says the family asked {D.him} to carry on the name, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"A letter from relatives exists. But no agency approved it.\""), .cross("Did {DL} hide the arrangement from relatives?", "\"Apparently not. Some relatives knew. That doesn't make it legal to claim benefits.\""), .cross("Did the family benefit from the claims?", "\"I can't say. I only know where the money went, which was to {D.him}.\""), .cross("The letter does not come from any agency, does it?", "\"No. It is from relatives only, and no agency ever approved a name swap.\""), .cross("{D} did not lie about family involvement, did {D.he}?", "\"No. {D.He} told me about the family arrangement from the start.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Cousin",
        defenseExam: [.direct("How are you related to {D}?", "\"We are cousins, and we grew up two streets apart. I know the family history well.\""), .direct("What happened when the relative died?", "\"The family met at my grandparents' house. The elders said the name should be kept alive, and {D} agreed to carry it.\""), .direct("Was that known in the family?", "\"Yes. Everyone knew {DF} used that name at work and at home. No one hid it.\""), .direct("Did you sign the family letter?", "\"Yes, years ago, as a witness to what the family had said. I did not know it would be used in court.\""), .direct("How did the defendant act around the family?", "\"Respectful, and proud of the family name. {D.He} said many times that it was an honor.\""), .direct("What did you know about benefits?", "\"Nothing. I never knew that benefits or a mortgage were involved.\""), .cross("No agency approved the use of that name, did it?", "\"Not that I know of. The family did not think of agencies.\""), .cross("You never asked a lawyer whether it was legal, did you?", "\"No. Nobody did. It was a family decision.\""), .cross("The relative who died could not consent, could the relative?", "\"No. The family spoke for the relative, and I see how that does not make it legal.\""), .cross("You knew the defendant had a warrant under another name, didn't you?", "\"I heard something about it later, after the investigation began.\""), .cross("A mortgage is a serious thing to sign in someone else's name, isn't it?", "\"Yes. I understand that now.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} took a dead relative's name for money.", "A family arrangement."),
        allocution: "\"I never meant to hurt anyone.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} had a warrant under {DL}'s own name.", "The relatives did ask."),
        defendant: [.direct("Why did you use the relative's name?", "\"The family asked me to carry on the name. I took it and lived under it. I thought it was a family matter.\""), .direct("Did you know it was illegal?", "\"Not really. I thought it was a way to honor the family. I never meant to cheat anyone.\""), .direct("What about the benefits and mortgage?", "\"I used the name I'd taken. I did not think of it as a trick. It was just who I was.\""), .direct("What happened when the relative died?", "\"The family was grieving, and our elders asked me to carry on the name so it would not disappear. I was young and I agreed.\""), .direct("How did you live as that person?", "\"I took the name for jobs and everything else, and I signed with that name for years. It became second nature.\""), .direct("Why did you have a warrant under your own name?", "\"I had missed a court date years earlier and was afraid. Using the other name felt safer.\""), .cross("You signed a mortgage with a dead person's number, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I did. I should have known better.\""), .cross("You claimed $140,000 in benefits, didn't you?", "\"Yes. Over many years. I thought it was mine.\""), .cross("No agency approved this, did it?", "\"No. We never asked. We kept it in the family.\""), .cross("You signed a mortgage using that number, didn't you?", "\"Yes, and I knew it was not the one I was born with.\""), .cross("You never told any agency about it, did you?", "\"No. We never asked, and I know I should have.\"")],
        openings: ("{D} used the name and number of a dead relative for twenty years to hold jobs, claim $140,000 in benefits, and take a mortgage. A bank flagged the file. The State will present the fraud investigator.", "The defense will point you to a family that asked {D} to carry on a name in honor of a relative, with no one deceiving anyone within the family."),
        closings: ("Twenty years under a dead relative's name, $140,000 in benefits, and a mortgage signed with a dead person's number. Benefits belong to the living who qualify.", "A family asked {D} to carry on a name. The State has not proved {D} meant to defraud, rather than honor a relative."),
        timeline: [(-9000, "The relative dies."), (-7000, "{D} takes the name."), (0, "A bank flags the file."), (30, "Charges.")],
        identified: "Benefit records.",
        aggravating: ["The offense was committed for pecuniary gain"],
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"],
        genders: ["D": .male, "V": .male])

    static let droneDropAtTheYard = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.droneDropAtTheYard",
        category: .drugs,
        headlines: ["Drone Flew Pills Over a Prison Fence", "Man Admits Building the Drone But Denies the Pills"],
        law: "deliverSchedII",
        threshold: 7,
        spec: "Delivered a Schedule II controlled substance, on or about {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: false,
        summary: "A drone carried a package of oxycodone pills over a prison fence on {DATE}. Officers traced it to {D}, who built it. {DL} says a customer rented the drone and never said what it carried.",
        state: [E(.forensic, 3, "Drone Memory Card", "Flight path from {D}'s street."), E(.forensic, 3, "Package Contents", "Pills in a sealed bag."), E(.digital, 2, "Order Message", "'Same route as last time.'")],
        defense: [E(.document, 1, "Rental Contract", "{DL} rented drones for photography.")],
        role: "Corrections officer",
        exam: [.direct("What happened at the prison on {DATE}?", "\"A drone carried a package of oxycodone pills over the fence. The pills were in a sealed bag.\""), .direct("How did you trace the drone?", "\"The drone's memory card shows a flight path from {D}'s street. {D.He} built the drone.\""), .direct("What does the order message say?", "\"'Same route as last time.' That suggests the flight had been done before.\""), .direct("How did the drop happen?", "\"A drone approached the yard at dusk, flew over the fence line, and dropped a small package near the recreation field. An inmate picked it up before staff could reach it.\""), .direct("What was in the package?", "\"A sealed bag with about forty oxycodone pills. We sent it to the lab for confirmation.\""), .direct("How did the drone lead you to {D}?", "\"A crashed drone's memory card gave a flight path that started on {D.his} street. {D.He} builds and rents drones, so we followed up.\""), .cross("{DL} says a customer rented the drone, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"A rental contract exists for photography. I can't say who the customer was.\""), .cross("Did you see {DL} launch the drone?", "\"No. I traced it from the flight path. I did not see anyone launch it.\""), .cross("Is the flight path unique?", "\"It starts near {DL}'s street. Other people live there. But the drone is {DL}'s.\""), .cross("Many people live on that street, don't they?", "\"Yes. Several people there fly drones. {D.his} rental business is the one that came up.\""), .cross("The message 'same route as last time' could have gone to anyone, couldn't it?", "\"It could. I only know it came from a phone that was tied to the rental.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Customer",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Do you rent drones from {DL}?", "\"Yes. I've rented from {D} before. It's a regular business.\""), .direct("What do you use them for?", "\"Photography and surveying. It's what the rental is for.\""), .direct("Did {DL} rent to you often?", "\"Often. {D.He} is reliable.\""), .direct("What do you rent from {D}?", "\"Drones for photography and land surveying work. I have rented from {DF} several times over the past two years for my business.\""), .direct("How does a rental go at the defendant's place?", "\"I sign a contract, pay cash, take the drone and a battery, and return it in a couple of days. It is quick and easy and nobody asks questions.\""), .direct("Did the defendant ever ask about your plans?", "\"Never. {D.He} asked only about the return date and whether I knew how to fly the model. That is all the conversation we ever had.\""), .cross("Did {DL} ask what you carried?", "\"Never. I was never asked. {D.He} just handed over the drone.\""), .cross("Did you fly one to the prison?", "\"I'm not going to answer about myself. I'm only here to say how rentals work.\""), .cross("Did {DL} know your plans?", "\"I don't believe so. I never told {D.him}.\""), .cross("You were not asked about the prison, were you?", "\"No, and I am not going to say more about myself on that subject. I am here only to describe how {D.he} runs the shop.\""), .cross("{D} did not know what each customer planned to do with a drone, did {D.he}?", "\"Not to my knowledge. {D.He} never asked me, and I never told {D.him}, and I assume it was the same with other customers.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} flew drugs into a prison.", "A rental customer."),
        allocution: "\"I should have asked what was in it.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} had flown the route twice before.", "{DL} kept a rental log."),
        defendant: [.direct("What do you do with drones?", "\"I build them and rent them for photography. People hire them for pictures of events and properties.\""), .direct("Did you fly this drone to the prison?", "\"No. A customer rented it. The customer never said what it would carry.\""), .direct("What about 'same route as last time'?", "\"I don't know what that means. A customer may have used it before. I didn't ask.\""), .direct("How does your rental business work?", "\"Customers sign a contract, pick up a drone and a battery, and return it in two days. I do not ask what they plan to shoot.\""), .direct("Who rented this drone?", "\"A customer I knew only as a regular who rented several times. The customer paid cash and said it was for photography.\""), .direct("What did you do when deputies came?", "\"I showed them the rental contract and my log. I told them everything I knew.\""), .cross("The flight path started on your street, didn't it?", "\"That's where the rental started. The customer came to my place.\""), .cross("You didn't check what was carried, did you?", "\"No. I never do. I'm not supposed to inspect cargo.\""), .cross("You had flown that route twice before, hadn't you?", "\"I tested it in the past with a camera, because the street gets good light. I did not think it meant anything.\""), .cross("You built that drone, didn't you?", "\"Yes, it is one of mine. I did not know where it went on that day.\""), .cross("The order message says 'same route as last time.' You knew what that meant, didn't you?", "\"I knew the route, yes. I did not know what was in the package, and I should have asked after the first flight.\"")],
        openings: ("A drone carried oxycodone pills over a prison fence. The memory card shows a flight path from {D}'s street, and a message said 'Same route as last time.' The State will present the corrections officer.", "The defense will present a drone rental business, a customer who rented without telling {D} what it would carry, and no one who saw {D} fly it."),
        closings: ("A drone built by {D}, a flight path from {D}'s street, and a message about the same route as last time. Pills reached a prison.", "{D} rents drones to customers who never say what they carry. The State has not proved {D} flew it or knew its cargo."),
        timeline: [(-14, "First flight."), (0, "Drop at the yard."), (1, "Pills found."), (20, "Search of {DL}'s home.")],
        identified: "A flight path.",
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"],
        genders: ["D": .male])

    static let riggedMidwayGame = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.riggedMidwayGame",
        category: .whiteCollar,
        headlines: ["Carnival Operator Weighted Bottles So Prizes Could Not Be Won", "Dozens of Players Say the Game Was Fixed"],
        law: "falsePretenses",
        threshold: 6,
        spec: "Obtained money from others by false pretenses, on or about {DATE}.",
        ages: 21...65,
        victim: false,
        summary: "{D}, a midway operator, ran a ring toss and bottle game whose bottles were weighted on {DATE}. Players paid $5 per try. {DL} says the bottles were old, not rigged.",
        state: [E(.forensic, 3, "Bottle Weights", "Lead inserts in the base."), E(.video, 3, "Player Videos", "Perfect throws that never topple."), E(.document, 2, "Cash Counts", "$9,000 in a weekend.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Maker's Note", "{DL} shows a letter about heavy glass.")],
        role: "Fair inspector",
        exam: [.direct("What did you find when you inspected the game?", "\"Lead inserts in the base of the bottles. The bottles were weighted so they would not topple.\""), .direct("What do the player videos show?", "\"Perfect throws that never toppled the bottles. Players paid $5 per try.\""), .direct("How much did the game take in?", "\"$9,000 in a weekend. The cash counts show it.\""), .direct("What does your inspection involve?", "\"I check rides, games, and prizes for safety and fairness. For bottle games, I weigh bottles and compare them to the specs.\""), .direct("What did you find at {D}'s game?", "\"The bottles' bases were heavier than normal, with lead inserts tucked under a layer of tape. Each bottle weighed well over the standard.\""), .direct("How did you confirm players could not win?", "\"I tested the bottles with a standard ring and a bag of throws. Even perfect tosses barely moved them.\""), .cross("{D} says the bottles were old, not rigged, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"Yes. And a maker's note says bottles can be weighted. I will say it exists.\""), .cross("Did anyone ever win?", "\"Twice, I am told. That is a low number.\""), .cross("Could lead have been added for repair?", "\"Possibly, but not in that amount. It looked like a deliberate weighting.\""), .cross("Older glass bottles can be heavier, can't they?", "\"Yes, by a few ounces. These were weighted by more than that.\""), .cross("There was a maker's note about heavy glass, wasn't there?", "\"Yes, and it speaks to a thick base. It does not describe lead plugs.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Ride worker",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Did you add lead to the bottles at the game?", "\"Not me. I did not touch the bottles at all. {D} handled the bottles and set the whole game up.\""), .direct("Who handled the bottles day to day at the fair?", "\"{D.He} did. {D.He} set up the game each morning and kept all of the bottles in a bin at the booth.\""), .direct("Did you ever see lead in or around the bottles?", "\"No. I did not see any lead. I only saw the game running from my ride across the way.\""), .direct("What do you do at the fair?", "\"I run a ride on the midway, a few booths down from {D.his} game. I worked there all weekend.\""), .direct("What did you see at {D}'s game?", "\"{DF} set up the bottles in the morning and took them down at night. I did not see {DF} do anything to them.\""), .direct("How many winners did you see?", "\"Only two. The game seemed hard but fair.\""), .cross("Did you ever work the game yourself during the fair?", "\"No. I worked a ride the whole time. I was nearby, but I never ran the bottle game myself.\""), .cross("Did you watch players try to win at the game?", "\"Sometimes. Players rarely won, maybe twice that I saw. I did not keep any real count of it.\""), .cross("Did the defendant ever say anything to you about weighting the bottles?", "\"No. {D.He} never mentioned weights or lead to me. It was not something we talked about at all.\""), .cross("You never worked the game yourself, did you?", "\"No, I stayed on my ride.\""), .cross("You did not handle the bottles, did you?", "\"No, I never touched them.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} cheated players.", "Heavy old glass."),
        allocution: "\"I knew it was too hard.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} bought lead the week before.", "The maker's note is real."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you rig the game?", "\"No. The bottles were old, and I did not rig them. A maker's note says they came that way.\""), .direct("Why was there lead in the bases?", "\"For repairs. I patched the bases with lead to fix cracks. I did not do it to cheat.\""), .direct("Did anyone ever win?", "\"Twice. I handed out prizes both times.\""), .direct("How long have you worked the midway?", "\"Twenty years, running bottle and ring toss games. I keep my equipment as long as it holds up.\""), .direct("Where did you get the bottles?", "\"From an old supplier whose bottles are thick glass. I used a letter from the maker that says the bottles run heavy.\""), .direct("Why did you buy lead?", "\"I bought it for patching cracked bases on bottles that were wearing out. I only used a bit.\""), .cross("Lead bought the week before the fair. Isn't that planning?", "\"It was for repairs. I bought it for that purpose.\""), .cross("Perfect throws that never topple. How is that fair?", "\"The bottles are tricky. Maybe it was the angle.\""), .cross("$9,000 in a weekend and two winners. Doesn't that seem rigged?", "\"I can see why. It was not rigged by me.\""), .cross("Only two people won in a whole weekend, didn't they?", "\"Yes. It was a hard game, and I did not think that told anything.\""), .cross("Players paid $5 a try and almost nobody won, correct?", "\"Yes, most people do not win. That is how midway games work, but I understand why the weights make it look like more than that.\"")],
        openings: ("A midway operator, {D}, ran a bottle game for $5 per try. An inspector found lead inserts in the bottle bases, player videos show perfect throws that never toppled them, and the game took in $9,000 in a weekend.", "The defense evidence will establish that the bottles were old, that a maker's note exists, and that the lead was used for repairs, not rigging."),
        closings: ("Lead in the bases, perfect throws that never toppled, two winners in a weekend, and $9,000 taken. A game that cannot be won is a scam.", "Old bottles, repairs, and a maker's note. The State must prove {D} weighted the bottles to cheat, and repairs are not fraud."),
        timeline: [(-7, "{DL} buys lead."), (0, "The fair opens."), (2, "Complaints."), (3, "Inspection.")],
        identified: "An inspection.",
        mood: .indifferent,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"])

    static let santaSuitIntruder = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.santaSuitIntruder",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Man in a Santa Suit Walked Into a Home During a Holiday Party", "Guests Thought It Was a Gag Until Jewelry Vanished"],
        law: "burglary2",
        threshold: 7,
        spec: "Broke and entered the dwelling of {V} with intent to commit larceny, on or about {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
