        summary: "{D}, dressed as Santa, walked into {V}'s home on {DATE}, mingled with guests and left with a jewelry box. {DL} says a host invited {D.him} to play Santa. Santa arrived at about 7 p.m., and the box was gone by 7:45 p.m. A matching ring was listed at a pawn shop the next day, and {D} was arrested two weeks later.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Doorbell Video", "Santa enters unannounced."), E(.forensic, 3, "Jewelry Box", "Prints on the lid."), E(.digital, 2, "Pawn Listing", "A matching ring sold within a day.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Invitation", "{DL} says a guest called {D.him}.")],
        role: "Host",
        exam: [.direct("What happened at your holiday party?", "\"A person dressed as Santa walked into my home at about 7 p.m., mingled with my guests, and by 7:45 my jewelry box was gone.\""), .direct("What does your doorbell video show?", "\"Santa entering unannounced. No one had told me a Santa was coming, and I never invited anyone to play the part.\""), .direct("What came of the investigation?", "\"Fingerprints on the lid of the jewelry box, and a matching ring listed at a pawn shop the next day. {D} was arrested two weeks later.\""), .direct("What was the party?", "\"A holiday open house for about forty people, with kids and neighbors. We had a cookie table and music, and I was greeting people at the door.\""), .direct("What did you see when Santa arrived?", "\"A person in a full suit and beard came to the front door at about seven. I assumed it was a surprise from a guest, so I let it go.\""), .direct("When did you notice the jewelry box missing?", "\"About 7:45, when a guest asked to see a family ring. I went to the bedroom and the box was gone from the dresser.\""), .cross("{D} says a host invited {D.him} to play Santa, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"Yes, that is what {DL} says. I did not invite {DL}, but other hosts at a big party might have.\""), .cross("Did you see the defendant take the jewelry box?", "\"No. I did not see anyone take it. I only noticed it was missing after the party began to thin out.\""), .cross("Could the fingerprints be there from an earlier time?", "\"I do not know. I have never seen {DL} before that night, so I do not see how.\""), .cross("You did not see Santa go into the bedroom, did you?", "\"No. The hallway was crowded, and I did not see where Santa went.\""), .cross("Several guests had been upstairs that evening, hadn't they?", "\"Yes. Some used the bathroom, and the coats were on a bed in that room.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Guest",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Did the host know the person dressed as Santa?", "\"No. The host did not know Santa and asked around the room to find out who had arranged it.\""), .direct("Who invited Santa to the party?", "\"I do not know. No one admitted it at the time, and I asked several guests before the party ended.\""), .direct("What did you see Santa do at the party?", "\"Santa walked around and shook hands. Later I saw Santa go toward the kitchen, and I did not see more.\""), .direct("What did you see at the party?", "\"A person dressed as Santa walked in and mingled, handing out candy to the kids. Everyone thought it was a surprise.\""), .direct("Who hired Santa?", "\"I do not know. I asked around, and no one claimed to have.\""), .direct("How long was Santa there?", "\"About forty-five minutes. Santa went upstairs once and came down with a bag.\""), .cross("Did anyone at the party say they had hired Santa?", "\"No. No one spoke up, and I did not hear about an invitation from any guest.\""), .cross("Did you see Santa leave with a bag?", "\"I think so. Santa went out through the kitchen carrying a bag, but I did not look closely.\""), .cross("How long was Santa at the party?", "\"About forty-five minutes. It felt longer, because Santa walked through several rooms.\""), .cross("You saw Santa leave through the kitchen, didn't you?", "\"I think so. A bag went out the back door.\""), .cross("You did not see Santa take anything, did you?", "\"No. I only saw a bag and a person in a red suit.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} entered a home to steal.", "An invited performer."),
        allocution: "\"I got carried away.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} left through the kitchen with a bag.", "No one confirms an invitation."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you walk into the home dressed as Santa?", "\"Yes, I did. A host invited me to play Santa, and I thought I was welcome at the party.\""), .direct("Did you take the jewelry box?", "\"No. I did not take it. I walked around, said hello, and left when I felt I had done my part.\""), .direct("What was in the bag you carried out?", "\"Costume props. I had a sack of toys and extra pieces of the costume with me, and I carried them out.\""), .direct("How did you come to dress as Santa?", "\"I do holiday gigs each year and had a call that day from someone at a party who said the host wanted a Santa for the kids.\""), .direct("Who called you?", "\"A person who gave a first name only. They said the party was on that street and to come around seven.\""), .direct("What did you do at the party?", "\"I walked in, greeted kids, took a few photos, and passed out candy. I left through the kitchen because the front was crowded.\""), .cross("No one else says they invited you, do they?", "\"No. I know that is a problem. I was told by someone at the door that I could come in.\""), .cross("Your fingerprints were on the lid of the jewelry box, weren't they?", "\"I may have touched things in the house. I do not remember touching that box, but I cannot say I did not.\""), .cross("A matching ring was sold within a day. Do you know anything about that?", "\"I do not. The ring in the listing is a different matter. A friend gave me a ring as a gift.\""), .cross("No one at the party remembers hiring you, do they?", "\"No, and I know that makes my story weak.\""), .cross("You carried a bag out through the kitchen, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I was cold and went out the back to get my coat and the bag. I did not think anyone would think anything of it.\"")],
        openings: ("A person dressed as Santa walked unannounced into {V}'s home at 7 p.m., mingled with guests, and left through the kitchen with a bag. By 7:45 a jewelry box was gone, and {D}'s prints were on its lid.", "By the end of this trial, the proof will show that {D} was told someone at the party wanted a Santa and that {D} played the part and took nothing."),
        closings: ("Santa entered unannounced, left by the kitchen with a bag, and the jewelry box was gone within forty-five minutes. {D}'s prints were on the lid, and a matching ring sold the next day.", "No one confirms who invited Santa, but no one saw {D} take anything either. A fingerprint in a crowded house is not proof of theft, and the State has more questions than answers."),
        timeline: [(0, "7 p.m.: Santa arrives."), (0, "7:45 p.m.: the box is gone."), (1, "Pawn listing."), (15, "Arrest.")],
        identified: "Doorbell video.",
        mood: .divided,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"],
        genders: ["D": .male])

    static let fortyDollarBankNote = SmallCases.make(
