        summary: "{D} handed a bank teller {V} a note on {DATE} demanding cash, written on the back of a deposit slip bearing {D.his} name. {DL} says {D.he} was tricked into writing it. The note was slid across at about 10 a.m., and the cash was taken two minutes later. The teller identified the slip the next day, and the drawer was short $1,900.",
        state: [E(.document, 3, "Deposit Slip", "Name, account and note."), E(.video, 3, "Lobby Camera", "{D} slides a note and takes cash."), E(.document, 2, "Teller Drawer", "$1,900 missing.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Stranger", "{DL} says someone in a car dictated the note.")],
        role: "Teller",
        exam: [.direct("What happened at your window at about 10 a.m. on {DATE}?", "\"{D} slid a note across demanding cash. I handed over money about two minutes later.\""), .direct("What was written on the note?", "\"It was a demand for cash, written on the back of a deposit slip that carried {D.his} name and account number.\""), .direct("How much was taken?", "\"$1,900. My drawer was short that amount. I identified the slip the next day.\""), .direct("How did the note arrive?", "\"{D.He} stepped to my window around ten, slid a folded deposit slip across the counter, and said nothing. I opened it and read a demand for all the cash in my drawer.\""), .direct("What did you do?", "\"I handed over $1,900 from my drawer, pressed the silent alarm with my knee, and watched {DL} walk out. The whole thing took about two minutes.\""), .direct("How did you identify the slip?", "\"The next day I pulled it from the evidence bag and saw {D.his} name and account number printed at the top. It was a slip from our own lobby.\""), .cross("{DL} says someone in a car dictated the note, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"I didn't see anyone in a car. I saw {D.him} at my window.\""), .cross("Did {DL} show a weapon?", "\"No. I didn't see one. The note was the threat.\""), .cross("Did {DL} seem nervous?", "\"Yes, a bit. {D.He} looked stiff. I can't say why.\""), .cross("You did not see a weapon, did you?", "\"No weapon. The note said I would be hurt if I did not comply, but I never saw anything in {D.his} hands.\""), .cross("{D} was alone at the window, wasn't {D.he}?", "\"Yes, alone, and the camera agrees. I did not see anyone else come in or leave with {DL}.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Bank manager",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Do you manage the bank branch?", "\"Yes. I'm the manager. I was in the building that day.\""), .direct("Was the slip real?", "\"Yes. It was a real deposit slip. It had {D}'s name and account on it.\""), .direct("Did you review the video?", "\"Yes. I saw {DF} slide the note and take the cash.\""), .direct("What did you see on the video of the lobby?", "\"{D.He} walks in alone, goes to the window, slides a slip across, waits for the cash, and leaves. It takes about two minutes in total.\""), .direct("What was on the deposit slip?", "\"{D.his} name and account number printed at the top, and a handwritten demand on the back. It is a slip from our own branch.\""), .direct("What did you do after the robbery?", "\"I called deputies, secured the lobby, and checked on the teller. We reviewed all of the video before the deputies arrived.\""), .cross("Was anyone else with {DL}?", "\"No. {D.He} was alone on the camera.\""), .cross("Was anyone in a car outside?", "\"I don't know. The camera didn't show one. I can't say.\""), .cross("Did {DL} threaten anyone?", "\"Not with words. The note did the work.\""), .cross("No one else is shown in the lobby with {D}, are they?", "\"No. {DF} is the only person at the window, and the parking lot camera does not show a second person nearby.\""), .cross("A robber would hardly write a real name on a note, would they?", "\"It is unusual, and I noticed that myself. It either means carelessness or something else I do not know.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} robbed a bank teller.", "A dictated note."),
        allocution: "\"I was desperate.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} was alone on the camera.", "No one else is seen in the car."),
        defendant: [.direct("Why did you write the note?", "\"Someone in a car told me what to write. I was told to do it or something bad would happen. I wrote it on a slip I had.\""), .direct("Who was in the car?", "\"I don't know. I was scared. I didn't see faces clearly. I did what I was told.\""), .direct("Did you want the money?", "\"No. I took the money because I was afraid. I handed it over right after.\""), .direct("What happened before you came to the bank?", "\"I was parked in a lot when someone leaned into my car window and told me to write down a note on a slip. The person had a hand inside a jacket and sounded dangerous.\""), .direct("What did the person say to write?", "\"That I wanted all the cash in the drawer and that it was a robbery. I wrote it on the back of a deposit slip I had in my glove box.\""), .direct("What did you do with the money?", "\"I handed it to the person at the car door and drove off. I never counted it, and I never spent it.\""), .cross("The slip carries your name and account number, doesn't it?", "\"Yes. It was a slip I had. I know that makes it easy to trace.\""), .cross("You took $1,900, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I took the cash the teller handed me. I am truly sorry.\""), .cross("Nobody else is seen in the car, are they?", "\"I've heard that. I don't know. It felt like someone was watching.\""), .cross("Nobody else appears in the car footage, do they?", "\"I have heard that. I did not look around, and I was too frightened to turn my head.\""), .cross("You signed your own name and account number on the slip, didn't you?", "\"It was the slip I happened to have. It was pre-printed with my details, and I did not think about that.\"")],
        openings: ("A bank teller was handed a note demanding cash, written on a deposit slip with {D}'s name and account number. The lobby camera shows {D} sliding the note and taking $1,900. The State will present the teller and the video.", "The defense will point you to a person who says someone in a car dictated the note, acted under fear, and used a slip that obviously identified {D.him}."),
        closings: ("A note on a slip with {D}'s own name, a lobby camera, and $1,900 taken. {D} walked into a bank and demanded cash.", "No robber writes a name and account number on a note unless something is wrong. The State has not proved {D} acted freely."),
        timeline: [(0, "10 a.m.: the note."), (0, "10:02 a.m.: the cash."), (1, "Teller IDs the slip."), (2, "Arrest.")],
        identified: "A deposit slip.",
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"],
        genders: ["D": .male])

